01:06:38.110 --> 01:06:42.510
and checks were found in the hands of pretty clearly unsavory characters, Slim Buller and others,

01:06:42.670 --> 01:06:43.930
he was called into your office.

01:06:44.250 --> 01:06:48.230
Michael characterized the two-and-a-half-hour meeting as being about a half-hour worth of substance

01:06:48.230 --> 01:06:52.670
and the rest just for show, so it could look like the NBA was being tough on him.

01:06:52.930 --> 01:06:56.750
And he assured the league that there were no other checks out there and nothing else bouncing around.

01:06:57.010 --> 01:06:58.710
That turns out perhaps not to be true now.

01:06:58.710 --> 01:06:59.970
He assured the league.

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:05.520
league that he understood the gravity of the quality of his associations.

01:07:06.620 --> 01:07:08.820
We had quite a conversation on that subject.

01:07:09.080 --> 01:07:12.820
It probably didn't have to take more than five minutes, but it took considerably more

01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:13.220
than that.

01:07:13.540 --> 01:07:17.500
And we got certain assurances from him on that subject, and we'll be following up with him

01:07:17.500 --> 01:07:17.840
on that.

01:07:18.460 --> 01:07:22.460
There's a perception out there, not unanimous, but a perception that's somewhat widespread

01:07:22.460 --> 01:07:25.200
that the league is reluctant to discipline Jordan.

01:07:25.420 --> 01:07:26.420
Is that your perception?

01:07:26.700 --> 01:07:28.620
No, it's a perception that's out there that you hear.

01:07:28.620 --> 01:07:29.900
You know, there are too many times.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:31.900
in the course of these finals when people have said

01:07:31.900 --> 01:07:33.640
I don't say but they say

01:07:33.640 --> 01:07:35.340
he says and there's a perception

01:07:35.340 --> 01:07:36.800
the perception is that

01:07:36.800 --> 01:07:39.760
this league takes care of a variety

01:07:39.760 --> 01:07:41.700
of problems and a good

01:07:41.700 --> 01:07:43.800
question has been raised about gambling

01:07:44.500 --> 01:07:45.740
I have a concern

01:07:45.740 --> 01:07:48.100
but the problem is morals have changed

01:07:48.100 --> 01:07:50.250
in the last 30 years or so

01:07:50.250 --> 01:07:51.870
40 states promoted

01:07:51.870 --> 01:07:53.690
we've got casino gambling all over

01:07:53.690 --> 01:07:55.810
and that perception that you talk about

01:07:55.810 --> 01:07:58.070
is fueled in part by people saying

01:07:58.070 --> 01:07:59.900
that players shouldn't even

01:08:00.030 --> 01:08:08.150
frequent casinos. Well, that can't be. It's legal, and I'm not about to go rushing off to enact a

01:08:08.150 --> 01:08:14.840
series of rules. Not all high-stakes gambling is legal. That's true. So it could be a possible

01:08:14.840 --> 01:08:20.510
concern. And let me clarify here. No one wants to put excessive heat on Michael Jordan. He is a

01:08:20.510 --> 01:08:24.730
good guy as well as a great player. And most people are sympathetic to the invasion of privacy

01:08:24.730 --> 01:08:29.230
issues, the extraordinary scrutiny he's under, the fact that people can exploit his name and the names

01:08:29.230 --> 01:08:29.650
of others.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:35.580
similar positions but somewhere within all this tabloid stuff there is a legitimate issue yes i

01:08:35.580 --> 01:08:42.820
agree the legitimate issue is the association of players and the and the question of who they

01:08:42.820 --> 01:08:48.620
associate with and what it does with respect to the league uh and uh you know what steps the league

01:08:48.620 --> 01:08:54.240
should take uh to deal with that subject uh i'm just a little sensitive on the subject of uh

01:08:54.240 --> 01:08:59.980
the course of perceptions i mean we try to deal very directly with a number of concerns here

01:09:00.190 --> 01:09:03.130
And we'll deal with the issue of gambling as well.

01:09:03.290 --> 01:09:05.870
