They won during the course of the regular season,

02:14:12.010 --> 02:14:15.970
and they won three straight in the playoffs.

02:14:16.350 --> 02:14:19.430
What an unusual series this has been,

02:14:19.490 --> 02:14:23.730
with the Bulls winning the first two here in Phoenix,

02:14:23.830 --> 02:14:26.900
and then Chicago having their props at home.

02:14:26.920 --> 02:14:29.460
Phoenix winning two out of three at Chicago Stadium.

02:14:30.960 --> 02:14:37.540
credit to the the inner strength of both of these teams to be able to go on the road and win the big

02:14:37.540 --> 02:14:42.700
basketball games that they had to win to give themselves a chance to survive in this series

02:14:42.700 --> 02:14:48.400
you think it's over early when chicago takes the first two in this building and then phoenix goes

02:14:48.400 --> 02:14:54.360
back into the stadium makes a few adjustments grows as a team suddenly walks out of there with

02:14:54.360 --> 02:14:59.880
two victories now the momentum swings they work all year to get home court advantage with 62 wins

02:15:00.120 --> 02:15:02.980
Have game six and seven here, and what does Chicago do?

02:15:03.380 --> 02:15:07.010
Find the inner strength to come back and win the game they had to win here.

02:15:07.230 --> 02:15:11.510
I don't know anyone that wanted on Chicago's team to let it go to seven and take a chance.

02:15:11.710 --> 02:15:17.030
Mike, following tonight, we are czarless for all of us here at NBC Sports.

02:15:17.030 --> 02:15:23.890
We wish you the very best, the terrific three years for you, and the very best for the Cleveland Cavaliers.

02:15:24.050 --> 02:15:29.960
Remember, if things don't work out here at NBC, there are many behind-the-scenes.

02:15:30.000 --> 02:15:35.680
type jobs with the proper giving it the proper time I think that you know we'd

02:15:35.680 --> 02:15:39.560
accept your back I appreciate the encouragement all along the three years

02:15:39.560 --> 02:15:44.460
of solid encouragement so those are heads to Cleveland the Chicago Bulls are in

02:15:44.460 --> 02:15:48.760
the midst of celebrating and we will have the trophy presentation that is

02:15:48.760 --> 02:15:56.160
coming up shortly the Bulls make it three in a row we'll be right back well we

02:15:56.160 --> 02:15:59.400
have played this scene before and amid the bedlam of the visitors

02:16:00.090 --> 02:16:06.510
Phoenix, we have virtually the entire roster of the three-time champions, and David Stern will attempt to make the presentation.

02:16:06.730 --> 02:16:07.270
Go ahead, Commissioner.

02:16:07.510 --> 02:16:12.630
Three-time NBA world champion Chicago Bulls. Congratulations. It's a great accomplishment.

02:16:21.680 --> 02:16:24.780
Michael, we'll allow you to speak first on behalf of your teammates.

02:16:25.440 --> 02:16:29.880
Well, I think everybody put their effort out there. You know, from Corey Williams to Ed Nilo.

02:16:30.000 --> 02:16:31.360
All the guys that were going to the injury reserve.

02:16:31.700 --> 02:16:33.780
You know, this is a hard-fought three-peat.

02:16:33.900 --> 02:16:34.200
You know what I mean?

02:16:34.260 --> 02:16:35.060
It took a lot of work.

02:16:35.530 --> 02:16:38.030
A lot of times it looked kind of dim, but we stuck in there.

02:16:38.110 --> 02:16:41.910
We hung together as a team, and, you know, this is a reward of what the hard work does for you.

02:16:42.620 --> 02:16:45.000
The crowd here kind of blocks us from seeing the monitor.

02:16:45.160 --> 02:16:50.860
We'll try, but until Pax's winning three-pointer, you had all the points for the Bulls in the fourth quarter.

02:16:51.060 --> 02:16:52.480
I knew Pax was going to make that.

02:16:52.620 --> 02:16:53.920
I just knew whenever he got it.

02:16:54.220 --> 02:16:55.100
It was a great draw.

02:16:55.780 --> 02:16:58.400
And, you know, for my part, I just try to do whatever I can.

02:16:58.680 --> 02:16:59.860
I hope you enjoy it, Bob.

02:17:00.320 --> 02:17:01.620
It feels good right now.

02:17:01.840 --> 02:17:04.560
Is it joy or is it relief or is it a combination?

02:17:04.560 --> 02:17:06.620
This has been a great year but a tough year.

02:17:06.820 --> 02:17:07.300
It's both.

02:17:07.500 --> 02:17:09.800
It's a relief plus it's great to win.

02:17:10.020 --> 02:17:11.320
I think we've gone through a lot.

02:17:11.520 --> 02:17:13.400
Me personally, I've gone through a lot of ups and downs.

02:17:13.620 --> 02:17:16.530
But to cap it off this way means a lot to me.

02:17:16.650 --> 02:17:16.890
Believe me.

02:17:17.470 --> 02:17:20.830
I hate to make you look ahead, but you've talked about retirement in a year or two.

02:17:20.950 --> 02:17:22.730
Could you step aside if the streak is still intact?

02:17:23.410 --> 02:17:23.610
No.

02:17:24.070 --> 02:17:25.750
My love is strong for this game right now.

02:17:25.830 --> 02:17:26.710
That's how I'm looking at it.

02:17:26.790 --> 02:17:28.430
And I'm going to be here as long as my love is strong.

02:17:29.070 --> 02:17:29.890
We're going to roll inside.

02:17:30.000 --> 02:17:33.800
of the plays from the fourth quarter i don't know if we'll be able to see them try and make a little

02:17:33.800 --> 02:17:39.390
space here guys for michael to take a look and the one that i'd specifically like to talk about

02:17:39.390 --> 02:17:44.070
and we'll get to it in a minute would be your last basket they're up by four when frankie johnson

02:17:44.070 --> 02:17:48.570
misses a jump shot and they let you go the length of the floor used a very little time and they never

02:17:48.570 --> 02:17:53.110
touched i don't think anybody saw me you know i think once i got the rebound everybody was running

02:17:53.110 --> 02:17:57.890
to the three-point shooters you know i just kept putting pressure on the defense and right before

02:17:57.890 --> 02:17:59.350
I get to go to the basket for the layup.

02:17:59.450 --> 02:17:59.970
Scottie Pippen.

02:18:00.000 --> 02:18:01.960
grabs Marley, but you can't get to

02:18:02.440 --> 02:18:03.800
the basket and try to stop me.

02:18:03.900 --> 02:18:06.080
So that was a big play. Now on the last play,

02:18:06.140 --> 02:18:08.160
you had to give it up in the backcourt. Never touched

02:18:08.160 --> 02:18:09.920
it in shooting range. Pippen gave it to

02:18:09.920 --> 02:18:12.220
Horace and then back to Pax. Well, the plan

02:18:12.220 --> 02:18:14.060
was to get the ball to me, get it to

02:18:14.060 --> 02:18:16.100
Scottie, and cut off to Scottie. If I can get

02:18:16.100 --> 02:18:18.000
the ball back, get the ball back. But he

02:18:18.000 --> 02:18:20.120
turned it around, gave it to Horace, and then

02:18:20.120 --> 02:18:22.110
Horace kicked it back out to Paxson. And once

02:18:22.110 --> 02:18:24.290
I saw Paxson get the basketball, I knew it was good.

02:18:25.410 --> 02:18:26.050
Where is

02:18:26.050 --> 02:18:26.810
John Paxson?

02:18:28.070 --> 02:18:29.930
Where's Paxson? Move him in here.

02:18:31.740 --> 02:18:35.640
A couple of years ago, you scored 10 points on clutch jumpers in Los Angeles

02:18:35.640 --> 02:18:36.780
and what turned out to be the winner.

02:18:36.880 --> 02:18:41.420
You had a big fourth quarter against Portland as well in the sixth game last year.

02:18:41.540 --> 02:18:43.260
And now, the shot that wins the championship.

02:18:43.600 --> 02:18:45.140
Yeah, I'm just, this is a dream.

02:18:45.320 --> 02:18:45.880
What can I say?

02:18:46.600 --> 02:18:48.660
Maybe we were the ones destined to win after all.

02:18:48.920 --> 02:18:49.980
It was a great feeling.

02:18:50.100 --> 02:18:51.240
I can't describe what I feel.

02:18:52.170 --> 02:18:55.150
Before we continue, Michael, I know you want to jump down.

02:18:55.540 --> 02:18:59.720
This has been in many ways your year with the dream team and with the certification.

02:19:00.000 --> 02:19:01.840
in the minds of most now as the greatest

02:19:01.840 --> 02:19:03.880
to ever play the game. A final thought

02:19:03.880 --> 02:19:05.740
on what this means to you and your team.

02:19:06.000 --> 02:19:08.060
Well, I think it means a lot to us

02:19:08.060 --> 02:19:09.460
because we make history.

02:19:10.260 --> 02:19:11.700
Very few teams have done this.

02:19:12.040 --> 02:19:14.020
Especially when there's so much parity in the league

02:19:14.020 --> 02:19:15.780
right now. It's a major accomplishment

02:19:15.780 --> 02:19:17.220
for the franchise and for the team.

02:19:17.360 --> 02:19:20.060
For me personally, I think it's something

02:19:20.060 --> 02:19:21.940
that I was looking forward to, to separate

02:19:21.940 --> 02:19:23.280
myself from Magic and Bird.

02:19:23.620 --> 02:19:25.160
They never did it and I did it.

02:19:25.360 --> 02:19:28.110
That makes me feel special.

02:19:28.230 --> 02:19:29.310
I believe it. Congratulations.

02:19:30.000 --> 02:19:36.220
Pax. All right, let's go back to Pax. When it left your hand, your thoughts? I mean, you had the stroke going, no doubt about it.

02:19:36.280 --> 02:19:42.240
I don't know. That's instinct. You catch and you shoot. I've done it hundreds of thousands of times in my life.

02:19:42.400 --> 02:19:47.700
So Horace gave me a good pass. We struggled that fourth quarter. I'm just glad I could do something about it.

02:19:47.880 --> 02:19:50.760
You were spotting up the whole play. That was obvious. You just went to that spot.

02:19:50.900 --> 02:19:55.260
Right. I was going to stay behind the three-point line in case something happened, and the ball just fell in the Horace's hands.

02:19:55.260 --> 02:19:59.840
I got it. Unbelievable. I'm glad Chicago's got a third one. We're a city of champions.

02:20:00.580 --> 02:20:01.280
Congratulations, John.

02:20:01.380 --> 02:20:01.480
Thank you, Bob.

02:20:01.580 --> 02:20:02.060
I appreciate it.

02:20:02.160 --> 02:20:03.840
All right, we'll be back, and we'll talk with Phil Jackson.

02:20:04.140 --> 02:20:04.280
Oh, wait.

02:20:04.400 --> 02:20:06.000
Michael has an additional thought.

02:20:06.080 --> 02:20:06.240
Go ahead.

02:20:06.240 --> 02:20:08.080
This is for Jasmine, my sweet little daughter.

02:20:08.160 --> 02:20:08.540
Who you with?

02:20:08.700 --> 02:20:09.860
Happy birthday, Jazz.

02:20:10.220 --> 02:20:12.260
And happy Father's Day to Michael Jordan.

02:20:12.260 --> 02:20:12.540
Happy Father's Day, everybody.

02:20:13.040 --> 02:20:13.520
All right.

02:20:13.900 --> 02:20:14.640
Trent Tucker's here.

02:20:14.740 --> 02:20:15.800
Daryl Walker, Horst Grant.

02:20:15.920 --> 02:20:17.040
Bill Cartwright, Scotty Pippen.

02:20:17.120 --> 02:20:18.380
We'll talk with the coach, Phil Jackson.

02:20:18.620 --> 02:20:21.180
But first, let's go over to the Phoenix locker room.

02:20:21.260 --> 02:20:22.940
Paul Westphal is with Hannah Storm.

02:20:24.380 --> 02:20:28.200
Coach, a great effort by your team, and you came so close to taking this to a seventh game.

02:20:28.320 --> 02:20:29.960
Can you describe what happened on the final play?

02:20:30.000 --> 02:20:31.840
when John Paxson sunk the three-pointer?

02:20:33.060 --> 02:20:36.540
Well, it was just a spread court situation.

02:20:36.540 --> 02:20:37.900
They tried to take it to the basket,

02:20:37.900 --> 02:20:41.780
and Mark West had to leave Horace Grant to go help on the penetration,

02:20:41.860 --> 02:20:45.520
and Danny Ainge thought that he might be able to pick the pass off,

02:20:45.680 --> 02:20:47.620
and instead of throwing it to Grant,

02:20:47.760 --> 02:20:50.380
he turned and passed it back to Pippen, who was wide open.

02:20:50.600 --> 02:20:52.540
I mean back to Paxson, who was wide open.

02:20:52.960 --> 02:20:55.640
It seemed like that ball was in the air for about an hour,

02:20:56.480 --> 02:20:58.900
and he made the shot.

02:20:59.020 --> 02:20:59.860
It's a great shot.

02:21:00.000 --> 02:21:01.000
You've got to give them credit.

02:21:02.860 --> 02:21:06.560
It's something every kid dreams about, and John Paxson got to live that dream out.

02:21:07.140 --> 02:21:08.900
Coach, what about the dreams of your team?

02:21:09.040 --> 02:21:10.380
I know that they are very disappointing.

02:21:10.380 --> 02:21:11.680
What did you tell them after the loss?

02:21:12.330 --> 02:21:13.550
Well, I wasn't real articulate.

02:21:13.810 --> 02:21:16.530
I just told them that I was very proud of them,

02:21:16.650 --> 02:21:23.150
that they gave me everything that they had, and that they lost to a great team.

02:21:23.980 --> 02:21:24.520
Thanks, Coach.

02:21:24.740 --> 02:21:27.850
Congratulations on a great season in your first year, and we'll see you next year.

02:21:28.190 --> 02:21:28.550
Bob?

02:21:31.600 --> 02:21:33.660
All right, thank you, Hannah. We just heard Paul Westfall

02:21:33.660 --> 02:21:35.580
say, Phil, we lost

02:21:35.580 --> 02:21:37.500
to a great team. I think it was better

02:21:37.500 --> 02:21:39.560
for history's sake, now that you got it, that they proved

02:21:39.560 --> 02:21:42.080
to be such a stern test. Well, we never

02:21:42.080 --> 02:21:43.780
could get a hold of this basketball club.

02:21:43.920 --> 02:21:45.940
You know, we've always been able to defend somebody,

02:21:46.080 --> 02:21:47.880
put the claws on them and hold them down. We

02:21:47.880 --> 02:21:50.100
couldn't hold this team down. They found ways to squiggle

02:21:50.100 --> 02:21:51.980
out. They came back at you all

02:21:51.980 --> 02:21:54.060
the time. We had a nice lead. All of a sudden

02:21:54.060 --> 02:21:56.040
their defense took over in the fourth quarter. We were so

02:21:56.040 --> 02:21:57.860
fortunate to come out of that game with an opportunity

02:21:57.860 --> 02:21:59.920
win. You know, you scored 12 points in the

02:22:00.000 --> 02:22:02.060
fourth quarter, that's the lowest fourth quarter in a final

02:22:02.060 --> 02:22:04.000
since the advent of the 24-second clock, and you

02:22:04.000 --> 02:22:06.020
got away with it. Isn't that amazing? We got away and won.

02:22:06.160 --> 02:22:08.020
We had five points with three-something left on

02:22:08.020 --> 02:22:10.080
the clock. I told the guys, we'll find a way to win.

02:22:10.320 --> 02:22:11.940
We'll get this thing over. If you'll play

02:22:11.940 --> 02:22:13.680
defense, we'll do it. And they did it. It was great.

02:22:13.880 --> 02:22:15.940
How tough was this year for you, with Michael

02:22:15.940 --> 02:22:18.140
and Scotty coming off the Dream Team, guys tired

02:22:18.140 --> 02:22:19.740
perhaps mentally as well as physically?

02:22:20.350 --> 02:22:22.330
Well, we submitted a record for the fact that

02:22:22.330 --> 02:22:24.370
we wanted guys healthy in the playoffs, and it worked

02:22:24.370 --> 02:22:26.270
for us. And when you got Scotty and Michael

02:22:26.270 --> 02:22:28.350
and Horace and the guys that have played together as a

02:22:28.350 --> 02:22:29.910
crew, you got a great chance.

02:22:30.000 --> 02:22:30.640
to win the playoffs.

02:22:30.840 --> 02:22:31.820
Those are great guys to coach,

02:22:31.900 --> 02:22:33.200
regardless of the energy level.

02:22:33.480 --> 02:22:35.340
We might have coached a little bit this year,

02:22:35.660 --> 02:22:37.440
but we had to, and we got away with it.

02:22:37.500 --> 02:22:39.840
We came into the playoffs full bore, ready to go.

02:22:40.060 --> 02:22:41.720
I know talk about all-time great teams

02:22:41.720 --> 02:22:42.740
is a parlor game,

02:22:42.880 --> 02:22:44.640
but you played on one of them in the Knicks

02:22:44.640 --> 02:22:46.360
and against great teams of that era,

02:22:46.360 --> 02:22:48.700
and you coached one of them and against them,

02:22:48.720 --> 02:22:49.680
so you have a good perspective.

02:22:49.900 --> 02:22:50.760
Where does this club rank?

02:22:51.330 --> 02:22:52.250
Well, with Michael Jordan,

02:22:52.370 --> 02:22:53.710
you just step above everybody else

02:22:53.710 --> 02:22:55.230
because he's got such a will to win.

02:22:55.230 --> 02:22:56.010
He's so competitive.

02:22:56.150 --> 02:22:58.150
He helps everybody out to the nth degree,

02:22:58.210 --> 02:22:59.970
and that's what makes this team very,

02:23:00.000 --> 02:23:03.880
very special is they've got a guy a leader that's a great competitor they've got some great veterans

02:23:03.880 --> 02:23:09.380
like a paxton a bill and horace and scotty that fit together well and bjo came on this year had

02:23:09.380 --> 02:23:13.860
some guys off the bench that play their role but he has lifted us to another level so the sun's major

02:23:13.860 --> 02:23:18.180
missed the grateful dead concert in chicago this weekend but in a sense it's a grateful dead here

02:23:18.180 --> 02:23:22.100
grateful for the title and probably dead tired huh you bet we've been uh they've been playing

02:23:22.100 --> 02:23:28.080
for 30 years i can see them the next 30 years too congratulations phil thanks bob okay let's turn

02:23:28.080 --> 02:23:29.300
here to Horace Grant.

02:23:30.000 --> 02:23:32.760
Certainly offensively not a factor in the last couple of games,

02:23:32.940 --> 02:23:37.900
but the key block toward the end with Kevin Johnson on the final play.

02:23:38.040 --> 02:23:40.700
We're going to try to clear the monitor here so Horace can get a look at it

02:23:40.700 --> 02:23:42.440
and the pass out to Pax for the winner.

02:23:42.900 --> 02:23:45.360
Well, our free-throw shooting wasn't going right,

02:23:45.400 --> 02:23:46.580
but there's the block right there.

02:23:46.780 --> 02:23:49.900
I just wanted to get a hand up, and I got the ball.

02:23:51.020 --> 02:23:54.760
Did Barkley wear you out playing him at the defensive end?

02:23:54.820 --> 02:23:55.820
Did that hurt you offensively?

02:23:56.350 --> 02:23:59.970
I mean, I'm not an offensive player now, but Barkley...

02:24:00.000 --> 02:24:01.940
I mean, Gordon Barkley, you know, it really

02:24:01.940 --> 02:24:04.100
would wear anybody out. You know, it had a toll on me

02:24:04.100 --> 02:24:06.220
at the end. Scotty Pippen,

02:24:06.360 --> 02:24:08.720
you sliced down the lane on that last possession.

02:24:08.720 --> 02:24:10.840
It looked like the shot might have been yours. Then Horace

02:24:10.840 --> 02:24:12.760
was open, baseline, and he kicked it back

02:24:12.760 --> 02:24:14.810
out. Well, I felt like the horse

02:24:14.810 --> 02:24:16.810
was going to be open. I felt like his man was stepping in the

02:24:16.810 --> 02:24:18.910
lane, and I gave him the ball. I thought he was going to take

02:24:18.910 --> 02:24:20.930
it and finish it, but John Paxman

02:24:20.930 --> 02:24:22.890
was right there right open. I mean, what more

02:24:22.890 --> 02:24:25.740
can you say? No one can ever be the number

02:24:25.740 --> 02:24:27.600
one guy on this team except Michael Jordan,

02:24:27.600 --> 02:24:29.900
but in two consecutive clinchers, the fourth

02:24:30.000 --> 02:24:31.940
quarter against Portland in Game

02:24:31.940 --> 02:24:33.800
Six last year in Chicago, and here with the 23

02:24:33.800 --> 02:24:35.820
points on the 12 boards, you have made a key

02:24:35.820 --> 02:24:37.880
contribution, and in the Knicks series, you came

02:24:37.880 --> 02:24:39.900
up big when it was needed. So you've

02:24:39.900 --> 02:24:41.980
established yourself at a certain level.

02:24:42.320 --> 02:24:43.900
Our main focus is to go out and play hard

02:24:43.900 --> 02:24:45.940
and play our game and do what you can do on the

02:24:45.940 --> 02:24:48.140
court. Micah's going to beat Micah. Micah's

02:24:48.140 --> 02:24:49.800
going to get his 40, 50 points, but

02:24:49.800 --> 02:24:51.320
the rest of us contributed.

02:24:52.000 --> 02:24:53.940
We can do what we accomplished

02:24:53.940 --> 02:24:55.900
today, and tell me the truth. Did we just

02:24:55.900 --> 02:24:57.680
win three? You just won three.

02:24:59.100 --> 02:24:59.960
Gotta ask you one last

02:25:00.000 --> 02:25:01.740
Last thing, Barkley was really woofing at you.

02:25:01.820 --> 02:25:02.540
What was being said?

02:25:02.700 --> 02:25:03.780
Well, he was talking trash,

02:25:03.920 --> 02:25:05.400
said if you guys are going to be here to win,

02:25:05.500 --> 02:25:06.680
Steve, you guys are going to be here to win,

02:25:06.700 --> 02:25:07.660
so you want to come over for dinner.

02:25:08.140 --> 02:25:10.180
So I'm going to invite him to Chicago for dinner.

02:25:11.100 --> 02:25:11.420
Chicago!

02:25:16.090 --> 02:25:17.850
Let's turn to Bill Cartwright.

02:25:18.150 --> 02:25:20.270
At age 35, now the third in a row,

02:25:20.350 --> 02:25:21.670
they must become more and more precious

02:25:21.670 --> 02:25:23.630
because the sand is moving through the hourglass.

02:25:24.260 --> 02:25:25.020
Oh, no question.

02:25:25.220 --> 02:25:26.760
It's just unbelievable.

02:25:27.300 --> 02:25:29.720
I'm going to push you on us to win, to get it done.

02:25:30.030 --> 02:25:36.350
they're really kind of loose i tell you this i'm just an unbelievable effort huge shot by pax to

02:25:36.350 --> 02:25:42.010
get it done and here we are you played countless basketball games you can tell us the truth about

02:25:42.010 --> 02:25:45.590
this one when they had the ball up by four in less than a minute to go do you think you were

02:25:45.590 --> 02:25:50.580
coming back here wednesday there was a little doubt but you know any time you have michael jordan

02:25:50.580 --> 02:25:55.840
scotty pippen and packs were shooting the tar of the basketball you got a big chance so

02:25:55.840 --> 02:25:59.960
this was a huge game for us and for me and i feel it to death i'm going to

02:26:00.000 --> 02:26:02.060
say hello to my boys back home and my daughter.

02:26:02.820 --> 02:26:04.080
And a happy Father's Day

02:26:04.080 --> 02:26:06.060
as Will Perdue does the dowsing

02:26:06.060 --> 02:26:08.160
of Bill Cartwright. Let's go over to the other side. Much different

02:26:08.160 --> 02:26:09.980
atmosphere. KJ with Hannah Storm.

02:26:11.220 --> 02:26:12.980
Kevin, it was such a competitive series. Perhaps

02:26:12.980 --> 02:26:15.060
even more competitive than the final records will

02:26:15.060 --> 02:26:17.200
indicate. Four games to two. What was the difference

02:26:17.200 --> 02:26:18.780
in the end, do you think, between the two teams?

02:26:20.030 --> 02:26:21.210
I thought this last

02:26:21.210 --> 02:26:23.010
ball game was a great ball game. I thought I could have went

02:26:23.010 --> 02:26:25.110
either way. They got a pretty big cushion for

02:26:25.110 --> 02:26:27.030
three quarters, but we hung in there, cut the lead

02:26:27.030 --> 02:26:29.090
down in the fourth quarter, and they just made

02:26:29.090 --> 02:26:29.970
some big shots when they...

02:26:30.000 --> 02:26:33.380
needed it and you know certainly they deserve it you gotta give them a lot of credit. KJ a lot of

02:26:33.380 --> 02:26:37.360
people made the incorrect assumption that the NBA finals will be played in the east between the

02:26:37.360 --> 02:26:40.420
Knicks and the Bulls. Do you think that the Phoenix Suns by the way that they played in the

02:26:40.420 --> 02:26:44.480
finals gained a measure of respect? Well I think our play spoke for itself you know we're not

02:26:44.480 --> 02:26:49.060
satisfied with coming up short but this is our first our first goal run with the guys that we

02:26:49.060 --> 02:26:53.240
have on this team and one thing's for sure Charles is not gonna retire now we won't let him. And you

02:26:53.240 --> 02:26:59.960
won't either. No you're right. Okay KJ we'll see you next season. Bob? All right from KJ to BJ and you to

02:27:00.000 --> 02:27:01.960
You guys had a personal duel throughout this series.

02:27:02.260 --> 02:27:02.800
Well, it was.

02:27:02.900 --> 02:27:03.620
It was a challenge.

02:27:04.160 --> 02:27:05.960
If you want to be the best, you have to play against the best.

02:27:06.080 --> 02:27:07.420
And Kevin is a great guard.

02:27:07.440 --> 02:27:08.920
He's earned a lot of respect in this league.

02:27:09.040 --> 02:27:10.420
And I accepted the challenge.

02:27:10.420 --> 02:27:12.460
And I'm just glad that we prevailed as a team.

02:27:12.720 --> 02:27:14.340
You got a chance to start this year.

02:27:14.400 --> 02:27:16.780
And even with Pax's return, you stayed in the lineup.

02:27:16.780 --> 02:27:19.780
And you've managed on a team full of stars, a team that has Michael Jordan,

02:27:20.100 --> 02:27:21.520
to establish an identity of your own.

02:27:21.620 --> 02:27:23.460
Did you doubt that you'd be able to do that in the NBA?

02:27:23.920 --> 02:27:24.380
No, I didn't.

02:27:24.540 --> 02:27:25.720
I never doubted that I could do it.

02:27:25.760 --> 02:27:26.680
I know it's going to be very tough.

02:27:27.140 --> 02:27:29.980
I know I had to come out and work hard and overcome a lot of challenges.

02:27:30.000 --> 02:27:34.070
this year but the guy stuck with me and that was the most important thing and I'm just

02:27:34.070 --> 02:27:35.150
glad it all worked out for the best.

02:27:35.310 --> 02:27:36.230
B.J., congratulations.

02:27:36.530 --> 02:27:36.890
Thank you, Bob.

02:27:37.640 --> 02:27:40.520
We want to note that Charles Barkley has declined to speak with us.

02:27:40.640 --> 02:27:45.040
He is in the shower and he is very disappointed and we're going to have to leave the air now

02:27:45.040 --> 02:27:47.220
without hearing from Sir Charles.

02:27:47.400 --> 02:27:49.280
So, the wrap up here is pretty simple.

02:27:49.600 --> 02:27:53.390
The Bulls have three-peated, the nucleus of their club still fairly young.

02:27:53.570 --> 02:27:54.630
They still have the desire.

02:27:54.750 --> 02:27:57.950
Next year they'll try and come back perhaps and become the quad squad.

02:27:57.950 --> 02:27:59.750
For Marv Albert and Mike Fratello,

02:28:00.000 --> 02:28:05.080
Buckner, Vesey, Walton, Hannah Storm, Ahmad Rashad. I'm Bob Costas. So long from Phoenix.

02:29:42.470 --> 02:29:44.830
the courage and the toughness and the guts.

02:29:45.430 --> 02:29:47.650
And Pac's been hitting that shot for eight years

02:29:47.650 --> 02:29:49.010
and he hit it again when it counted.

02:29:49.350 --> 02:29:52.060
And guys just came back and got the stop they needed

02:29:52.060 --> 02:29:55.040
and just did the things that fundamentally sound things

02:29:55.040 --> 02:29:55.520
at the end.

02:29:56.460 --> 02:29:57.660
It's a great basketball team.

02:29:57.760 --> 02:29:58.720
It's a great bunch of guys.

02:30:00.280 --> 02:30:02.960
As great a team as it is, it's a greater bunch of people, John,

02:30:03.100 --> 02:30:05.660
and that's what makes it so special to me.

02:30:05.960 --> 02:30:08.560
You know, we came out here to play a team that was outstanding,

02:30:08.780 --> 02:30:10.380
excelling in three-point field goal shooting.

02:30:10.580 --> 02:30:15.440
Tonight, John Paxson, B.J. Armstrong, Michael Jordan, and Trent Tucker all filled it up.

02:30:15.980 --> 02:30:19.000
Yeah, just great display, and I just so tickled pink.

02:30:19.260 --> 02:30:21.480
John, why don't you get the players on there, the guys that did this.

02:30:21.940 --> 02:30:22.400
All right.

02:30:23.580 --> 02:30:25.820
Scotty Pippen, step in here and say to Sports Channel,

02:30:25.960 --> 02:30:27.700
Scotty, you got your third ring, baby.

02:30:27.740 --> 02:30:28.500
How's that going to feel?

02:30:29.320 --> 02:30:29.880
It's great.

02:30:30.160 --> 02:30:35.730
This thing has become a struggle this season.

02:30:36.370 --> 02:30:38.050
We got here with this Phoenix team today.

02:30:38.190 --> 02:30:41.570
We never could get a feel of them, but the big shot by Pax

02:30:41.570 --> 02:30:42.790
has really changed the whole atmosphere.

02:30:43.050 --> 02:30:47.490
You know, the long-range shooting by Pax, by B.J., by M.J.,

02:30:47.490 --> 02:30:49.810
and by Tucker really helped you guys out a little bit today, didn't it?

02:30:50.130 --> 02:30:51.990
Those guys are great shooters.

02:30:52.250 --> 02:30:55.110
I mean, they spread the defense out, and, you know,

02:30:56.910 --> 02:30:58.590
you can't just say enough about Pax.

02:30:58.690 --> 02:30:59.970
He's been coming off the bench now.

02:31:00.000 --> 02:31:02.240
out big shots for us all season, and the playoffs

02:31:02.240 --> 02:31:04.200
is always finds a way to set this game up.

02:31:04.480 --> 02:31:06.140
With them shooting outside like that,

02:31:06.300 --> 02:31:08.140
the team, you've got to respect them, and they didn't

02:31:08.140 --> 02:31:10.040
respect them. You're down by two. You've got about

02:31:10.040 --> 02:31:12.100
13 seconds. The ball is coming inbounds.

02:31:12.180 --> 02:31:14.020
What's going through your mind? That crowd's screaming

02:31:14.020 --> 02:31:15.860
and hollering. Hopefully

02:31:15.860 --> 02:31:18.080
they wasn't going to catch me in the lane behind

02:31:18.080 --> 02:31:19.940
Barkley, but Horst

02:31:19.940 --> 02:31:21.980
made a great defensive job on KJ. It was

02:31:21.980 --> 02:31:22.980
a great block, and

02:31:24.140 --> 02:31:25.680
the clock expired, and that's it.

02:31:25.780 --> 02:31:28.000
I'm not even asking if you're going to look for four. I know you are.

02:31:28.480 --> 02:31:28.800
Definitely.

02:31:28.800 --> 02:31:29.320
I don't know.

02:31:31.260 --> 02:31:35.440
Scottie Pippen, yes sir, one of the all-star games of his career.

02:31:35.860 --> 02:31:38.020
Scott Williams now handling the trophies.

02:31:38.160 --> 02:31:42.680
He's got his three fingers up with three world champions in the Chicago Browns.

02:31:54.940 --> 02:31:59.080
Now you're looking at the America West Arena inside.

02:32:00.000 --> 02:32:05.040
But not inside the locker room where Johnny Red Kerr gets the champagne bath.

02:32:05.280 --> 02:32:10.720
And we saw one of Norm's favorite teammates, Bob Butterbean, loving that shot also.

02:32:11.020 --> 02:32:12.990
And Norman, how about it?

02:32:13.880 --> 02:32:15.860
It's a feeling, man, I don't know.

02:32:16.020 --> 02:32:16.580
It's great.

02:32:16.720 --> 02:32:17.940
I can't explain it.

02:32:18.000 --> 02:32:18.540
It's just great.

02:32:18.700 --> 02:32:20.440
It was a long, hard battle getting there.

02:32:20.660 --> 02:32:21.780
They did it.

02:32:21.880 --> 02:32:25.920
I think this year is sweeter than the last two because of the injuries,

02:32:26.160 --> 02:32:29.980
the way they took about facing this championship, shifting over.

02:32:30.000 --> 02:32:34.240
The starting lineup with B.J., all those particular things just makes it all sweet,

02:32:34.320 --> 02:32:35.680
and they just did a heck of a job.

02:32:35.980 --> 02:32:38.340
More of a team effort, I think, this year than the last two.

02:32:38.660 --> 02:32:43.100
It's amazing that they overcame the injuries before the playoffs began.

02:32:43.320 --> 02:32:44.180
Horace was hurting.

02:32:44.380 --> 02:32:45.080
Scotty was hurting.

02:32:45.200 --> 02:32:46.060
Michael was hurting.

02:32:46.160 --> 02:32:48.300
He had the wrist injuries, the ankle injuries,

02:32:48.480 --> 02:32:52.420
Paxson and Cartwright with the knee injuries, but no injuries at the end.

02:32:52.480 --> 02:32:54.860
Just lots of smiles except for Bob Costas' eye.

02:32:55.000 --> 02:32:58.180
A little champagne there burning there in that video we just saw.

02:32:58.280 --> 02:32:59.960
Let's go back down to the America West.

02:33:00.000 --> 02:33:03.580
Arena. Julie Jettleson, Mike Goldberg on the scene. Guys, take it away.

02:33:04.420 --> 02:33:07.880
Well, thank you, Steve Cashel. It is quiet now. The Bulls have started their celebration.

02:33:08.000 --> 02:33:12.040
Quite a celebration it was, huh, Julie? Quite a celebration. In fact, Michael Jordan,

02:33:12.200 --> 02:33:16.400
happier than he has been in weeks since the gambling thing, since not talking

02:33:16.400 --> 02:33:19.720
to the media. And this is the first time a lot of people say they've actually seen him smile.

02:33:20.080 --> 02:33:24.060
Every question you're about to see in this interview is thrown at him about everything

02:33:24.060 --> 02:33:28.220
you can imagine under the sun. The ugly fourth quarter. He says, who cares? We won,

02:33:28.260 --> 02:33:29.960
and now we're on our way to a fourth champion.

02:33:32.240 --> 02:33:36.040
You know, Phil called the first one a honeymoon, the second one he called a...

02:33:36.040 --> 02:33:37.360
No, the first one was a honeymoon.

02:33:37.750 --> 02:33:38.790
The second one was an odyssey.

02:33:38.890 --> 02:33:39.350
What is history?

02:33:39.990 --> 02:33:40.350
History.

02:33:40.650 --> 02:33:42.150
Yeah, that's what it is, it's history.

02:33:42.330 --> 02:33:44.770
Were you getting to be overcome by history for a while there?

02:33:45.280 --> 02:33:51.680
Man, I was so nervous the last 3.9 seconds in my... more than my whole career, you know,

02:33:51.720 --> 02:33:55.620
because I just wanted it to happen for so many people, and I'm just so glad that it got over with.

02:33:55.800 --> 02:33:59.380
You know, when you first got up to the podium, you mentioned Ed Neely and Corey Williams.

02:33:59.520 --> 02:33:59.960
You wanted to...

02:34:00.480 --> 02:34:19.820
I talked to those guys all season long, I kept telling to them, I said, just hang on to my coattail, man, we're going to get to where we have to go, and I want you guys to get it, because you just came to this team, and we want everybody to be a part of a championship team, especially Joel Walker, Ed Neely, these guys have been in the league for so long, and never had that opportunity, and now they've got one to show for their careers.

02:34:19.920 --> 02:34:25.460
Remember I had to ask you, do you need to have this one, you had to have it because of such a controversial season this year?

02:34:25.460 --> 02:34:29.900
You guys call it a controversial, I think it's a maturing event for me, you know, I think

02:34:30.000 --> 02:34:32.460
My life has been to a point where, you know,

02:34:32.540 --> 02:34:34.740
I've exceeded everything that I could basketball-wise,

02:34:34.740 --> 02:34:38.080
and you guys are taking it even a step further trying to get into my private life.

02:34:38.200 --> 02:34:41.220
And, you know, I think the city of Chicago has supported me,

02:34:41.240 --> 02:34:42.980
my family and my friends have supported me,

02:34:43.000 --> 02:34:46.740
and I think this just means a lot to me just to get through this year

02:34:46.740 --> 02:34:50.960
and say, hey, you know, I'm a human, and yet humans, you know, make mistakes,

02:34:51.020 --> 02:34:53.060
but yet we bring championships to Chicago.

02:34:53.420 --> 02:34:56.240
Michael, a lot of us wanted to leave you alone, but, you know, we have to.

02:34:56.420 --> 02:34:59.100
You know, I respect a lot of you guys because you have to do your job.

02:35:00.000 --> 02:35:01.640
Some of you, I can care less about.

02:35:02.560 --> 02:35:03.380
Michael, are you satisfied?

02:35:03.380 --> 02:35:04.740
You're not one of them, believe me.

02:35:04.860 --> 02:35:05.960
Are you satisfied, Michael?

02:35:06.140 --> 02:35:07.720
I mean, three, that's enough, isn't it?

02:35:08.320 --> 02:35:08.880
Enough for who?

02:35:08.880 --> 02:35:09.000
You.

02:35:09.320 --> 02:35:10.020
Enough for you.

02:35:10.180 --> 02:35:11.040
No, it's never enough.

02:35:11.140 --> 02:35:13.840
It's never enough as long as you compete.

02:35:14.220 --> 02:35:16.160
You know, it's always great to win, but that's why you compete.

02:35:16.520 --> 02:35:19.960
And I think, you know, we're going to certainly try to do this for the fourth term.

02:35:20.560 --> 02:35:23.640
You know, but right now in the third term, there's a lot of damn work.

02:35:23.880 --> 02:35:25.120
How many more are you going to go for?

02:35:25.720 --> 02:35:26.700
As long as I'm playing.

02:35:26.920 --> 02:35:29.380
You know, I hate to come short.

02:35:29.580 --> 02:35:29.960
You know, come up.

02:35:30.000 --> 02:35:31.840
I'm sure you've done it three times in a row.

02:35:32.880 --> 02:35:34.600
I'd love to see us do it for the fourth time.

02:35:36.500 --> 02:35:37.120
Just get out.

02:35:37.220 --> 02:35:37.700
Just get out.

02:35:37.780 --> 02:35:38.540
You're not holding a mic.

02:35:38.680 --> 02:35:39.460
You said I wasn't?

02:35:39.540 --> 02:35:40.200
Yeah, for real.

02:35:40.560 --> 02:35:42.640
I never said I wasn't going to be back next year.

02:35:42.780 --> 02:35:44.940
I think, you know, don't jump to conclusions, man.

02:35:45.260 --> 02:35:46.400
Don't Wayne Gretzky me.

02:35:46.420 --> 02:35:49.000
That's the only thing the media can do, man, is jump to conclusions.

02:35:49.280 --> 02:35:50.040
See, that's...

02:35:50.460 --> 02:35:53.560
You said last one was the toughest because you went through so much.

02:35:53.820 --> 02:35:54.520
You know, I put a foot in my mouth.

02:35:54.520 --> 02:35:55.920
But this one, this is the toughest, right?

02:35:55.920 --> 02:35:56.660
I put a foot in my mouth.

02:35:56.820 --> 02:35:59.880
You know, beginning of the season, I do remember distinctively saying

02:35:59.880 --> 02:35:59.940
And then...

02:36:00.000 --> 02:36:02.300
that this is going to be a lot easier than the second one.

02:36:02.420 --> 02:36:03.760
But, you know, I'm totally wrong.

02:36:03.980 --> 02:36:09.650
You know, I know that, you know, the third one was so much, so much, so much work.

02:36:09.970 --> 02:36:14.430
And with all the other things thrown in there from, you know, the gambling,

02:36:14.690 --> 02:36:18.590
you know, all the different controversy just made it even more hard.

02:36:18.810 --> 02:36:20.490
Imagine how hard number four is going to be.

02:36:20.850 --> 02:36:22.610
Imagine how hard number four is going to be.

02:36:23.090 --> 02:36:25.310
If it's as gratifying as it is right now.

02:36:25.910 --> 02:36:28.750
Michael Jordan looks like you just won the Indy 500 changing hats.

02:36:29.050 --> 02:36:29.970
This is my Nike.

02:36:30.000 --> 02:36:34.460
job. Just did it. I mean, again, again, and again. Charles was saying that they were the team of

02:36:34.460 --> 02:36:38.240
destiny. It's quite clear you were. I mean, it looked like this game was totally taken away from

02:36:38.240 --> 02:36:43.060
you right at the end. I think Charles needed to go to church on Sunday. You know, destiny, I mean,

02:36:43.880 --> 02:36:48.340
anybody can have destiny. You know, it's not just one team or another team. It's whoever put the

02:36:48.340 --> 02:36:52.860
work ethic that's out there, you know, lay the work on the basketball court can be the team of

02:36:52.860 --> 02:36:57.700
destiny. And, you know, even though we look very dim, score 15 points in the fourth quarter, which

02:36:57.700 --> 02:36:59.960
It's kind of shocking, you know, but therefore...

02:37:00.000 --> 02:37:01.820
was there. And I guess we were the team of

02:37:01.820 --> 02:37:03.460
destiny this year, and that's what I told Charles.

02:37:04.080 --> 02:37:05.760
I told him I loved him, you know,

02:37:05.880 --> 02:37:08.040
but destiny must be next year.

02:37:08.120 --> 02:37:10.120
Do you think he really felt it was destiny, though?

02:37:10.340 --> 02:37:11.520
Yeah, he's going to pay from now on.

02:37:11.880 --> 02:37:13.760
If he thinks Marley's better than Jordan's,

02:37:13.760 --> 02:37:15.900
he's definitely going to pay. Do you think he thought it was destiny

02:37:15.900 --> 02:37:17.800
or he's just trying to psych you? I mean, it's a matter

02:37:17.800 --> 02:37:19.880
of motivation. Every player, every

02:37:19.880 --> 02:37:21.920
team needs certain motivation to get

02:37:21.920 --> 02:37:23.940
themselves to a certain point, and he

02:37:23.940 --> 02:37:25.860
used destiny as motivation for his team.

02:37:26.220 --> 02:37:27.980
We used it as, you know, as energy

02:37:27.980 --> 02:37:29.900
for us. You know, they may be destined, but

02:37:29.900 --> 02:37:29.980
Thank you.

02:37:30.220 --> 02:37:31.280
Not this year, they may not.

02:37:32.630 --> 02:37:35.750
You did something that Bird and Magic and Kareem never did.

02:37:35.890 --> 02:37:37.170
You were on the three-peat championship.

02:37:37.330 --> 02:37:39.610
That's got to be, of all the personal things that have happened to you,

02:37:39.670 --> 02:37:40.570
this has got to be right on the top.

02:37:40.630 --> 02:37:42.150
From an individual standpoint, you know,

02:37:42.210 --> 02:37:45.370
if I could take anything individually from what this team has accomplished,

02:37:45.370 --> 02:37:49.050
that would be the major individual award that I can see.

02:37:49.270 --> 02:37:52.470
You know, but from a team concept, you know, to win three in a row,

02:37:52.930 --> 02:37:57.190
when you've got 28 teams in this league, so much parity, so much talent in this era,

02:37:57.940 --> 02:37:59.760
I mean, you don't put us with one of the history teams.

02:38:00.410 --> 02:38:01.270
then forget you.

02:38:01.930 --> 02:38:04.390
What are you going to do now when you finally get away from us?

02:38:05.300 --> 02:38:07.940
Michael Jordan saying that last 3.9 seconds,

02:38:07.960 --> 02:38:10.420
he was as nervous as he's ever been in his career.

02:38:10.680 --> 02:38:14.220
The longest 3.9 seconds for probably anybody on this team,

02:38:14.360 --> 02:38:16.300
including General Manager Jerry Krause,

02:38:16.360 --> 02:38:20.480
who said that was the best $100,000 he's ever spent getting John Paxson over here.

02:38:20.700 --> 02:38:22.740
Nobody can get John Paxson out of their mind,

02:38:22.840 --> 02:38:24.040
including Bill Cartwright,

02:38:24.100 --> 02:38:28.020
who relayed the story of John Paxson's three-point shot to me.

02:38:29.060 --> 02:38:29.980
Tell us the future.

02:38:30.190 --> 02:38:31.690
when Jon Pax hit that three?

02:38:33.430 --> 02:38:34.590
The Giants at three.

02:38:34.950 --> 02:38:36.550
At first we kind of joked about it.

02:38:37.430 --> 02:38:41.290
Phil said, you know, do we want to go for the three?

02:38:42.250 --> 02:38:44.830
And it was kind of laughing, and then it kind of turned out

02:38:44.830 --> 02:38:48.670
where Horace ended up with the ball and flipped it over to Jon,

02:38:48.830 --> 02:38:52.650
and when he knocked it down, it was just incredible.

02:38:53.750 --> 02:38:56.670
I think if they would leave Jon open, or Jon would be open

02:38:56.670 --> 02:38:59.670
in that situation, they didn't knock down the shot, so...

02:39:00.030 --> 02:39:04.110
I think in that, that kind of, that lifted us over the top.

02:39:04.270 --> 02:39:07.970
That kind of took the air out of them, even though they had the last position.

02:39:08.570 --> 02:39:11.150
Horace was able to bat the ball away, and that was it.

02:39:11.390 --> 02:39:14.430
So it took, it just took playing out the game.

02:39:14.630 --> 02:39:17.410
You know, the game's never over until that last click of the clock is off.

02:39:17.810 --> 02:39:21.950
You know, we scrambled, and we may have not deserved the damn game, but we got it.

02:39:23.150 --> 02:39:26.190
So Bill Cartwright, much maligned by the press in this series,

02:39:26.290 --> 02:39:29.930
but everyone forgets he's the one with all his help against New York that got them here.

02:39:30.000 --> 02:39:32.660
So this is really a team win, and that's what Michael Jordan said

02:39:32.660 --> 02:39:34.880
and John Paxson and all the heroes of this series.

02:39:35.120 --> 02:39:37.400
You know, it's always interesting that when you get down to it,

02:39:37.520 --> 02:39:39.900
it comes down to the roles that different players play.

02:39:40.000 --> 02:39:43.420
And Stacey King was one of those guys who played his role throughout the series.

02:39:43.580 --> 02:39:45.000
He had some good offensive games.

02:39:45.060 --> 02:39:46.700
I believe it was against the Cleveland Cavaliers.

02:39:46.840 --> 02:39:50.600
So along the road, we must remember that it's not just the finals that were important,

02:39:50.660 --> 02:39:52.540
but it was the whole run that this team put together.

02:39:52.700 --> 02:39:55.440
And Stacey King does a very good Bill Cartwright impersonation,

02:39:55.460 --> 02:39:56.880
which he was doing all night.

02:39:56.940 --> 02:39:59.240
And Bill Cartwright, for the first time, wasn't throwing balls at him

02:39:59.240 --> 02:39:59.980
or yelling at him for doing it.

02:40:00.000 --> 02:40:03.280
I think Bill was enjoying the moment also as he was being made fun of.

02:40:03.360 --> 02:40:07.000
As a matter of fact, I caught up to Stacey King in the locker room before the team left earlier.

02:40:07.180 --> 02:40:08.660
Stacey King from earlier this evening.

02:40:09.160 --> 02:40:13.060
Very excited, Stacey King. Champagne tastes really good the third time around also, doesn't it?

02:40:13.100 --> 02:40:16.020
I'm just so excited. I'm just shaking. I just can't calm myself down.

02:40:16.360 --> 02:40:19.820
It was a big win for us. John Paxson hit a big shot.

02:40:20.200 --> 02:40:21.640
We didn't want to tie, but we wanted to win.

02:40:21.760 --> 02:40:25.880
That just shows you the guts of the Chicago Bulls in our city that we don't back down from nobody.

02:40:26.280 --> 02:40:28.460
How about winning all the games here in Phoenix?

02:40:28.460 --> 02:40:29.980
If I were to ask you before the series.

02:40:30.000 --> 02:40:34.860
If you guys were going to win all four games in Phoenix or all three games, check that, would you have said, oh, yeah, Mike?

02:40:35.450 --> 02:40:38.140
No. We would have been lying if we said we could have.

02:40:38.420 --> 02:40:42.540
We thought we'd come in here and at least get one or two split and go back home and finish it up.

02:40:42.740 --> 02:40:45.920
But it didn't turn out that way. We didn't play well at home.

02:40:46.020 --> 02:40:47.380
They came in and won two out of three games.

02:40:47.980 --> 02:40:51.540
But, hey, all I can say is it felt real good, and I'm just happy.

02:40:51.740 --> 02:40:56.500
You know, Bill Cartwright, I'm 62 years old. This might be my last season, but I'm enjoying the moment right now.

02:40:56.680 --> 02:40:59.540
It is a great moment. Hey, is it all coming to perspective yet?

02:40:59.540 --> 02:40:59.840
because

02:41:00.000 --> 02:41:03.620
It looked, from a viewer's point of view, that you guys were uptight.

02:41:03.800 --> 02:41:05.140
You guys were very determined, but uptight.

02:41:05.300 --> 02:41:06.060
Phoenix was having fun.

02:41:06.140 --> 02:41:07.480
Was the pressure on you today, Stace?

02:41:07.580 --> 02:41:08.660
No, the pressure wasn't on us.

02:41:08.700 --> 02:41:11.000
We came in here, we were really focused on what we had to do.

02:41:11.120 --> 02:41:12.900
We controlled the whole tempo of the whole game,

02:41:12.920 --> 02:41:15.680
except for the spurts in the fourth quarter when they got a little run on us.

02:41:15.880 --> 02:41:18.060
But I think our composure and our experience went out.

02:41:18.140 --> 02:41:20.540
We knew that with a minute and 30-something seconds ago in the game,

02:41:20.540 --> 02:41:21.760
we had two possessions left.

02:41:21.820 --> 02:41:23.160
All we had to do was take good shots.

02:41:23.320 --> 02:41:26.480
And Michael created those shots for the guys, and John Paxson stepped up big.

02:41:26.760 --> 02:41:27.740
He's going down in history.

02:41:27.800 --> 02:41:29.120
That's one remarkable shot.

02:41:29.120 --> 02:41:29.740
You

02:41:30.000 --> 02:41:31.600
are around John Paxson every day.

02:41:31.760 --> 02:41:34.140
He is about as classy a human being as there is.

02:41:34.360 --> 02:41:37.100
Isn't this apropos for a guy like that to hit a winning shot like this?

02:41:37.200 --> 02:41:37.600
It is.

02:41:37.700 --> 02:41:39.860
You know, if you look back on Paxson's career this year,

02:41:39.940 --> 02:41:41.780
he's had to go through two or three knee surgeries,

02:41:42.560 --> 02:41:44.400
then not making it in the starting lineup

02:41:44.400 --> 02:41:46.380
and accepting his role coming off the bench.

02:41:46.640 --> 02:41:49.300
He's been a team leader ever since I've been here my four years.

02:41:49.640 --> 02:41:52.060
And, I mean, when I grow up, I want to be like John Paxson.

02:41:52.220 --> 02:41:56.180
Not like Mike, but like John Paxson because John Paxson is the consummate pro.

02:41:56.340 --> 02:41:57.760
I mean, he comes to work hard every day

02:41:57.760 --> 02:41:59.880
and never has a bad thing to say about anybody.

02:42:00.000 --> 02:42:02.580
He just works hard, and he's a great role model for kids.

02:42:02.780 --> 02:42:05.200
I know you're going to enjoy this for a while, but I have to ask you.

02:42:05.320 --> 02:42:08.540
You guys have the kind of team that can come back and win a fourth straight.

02:42:08.740 --> 02:42:10.780
Will that have to enter your minds very soon?

02:42:11.270 --> 02:42:13.370
Well, you know, honestly, we're not going to be thinking about that.

02:42:13.450 --> 02:42:15.510
We don't want to put our foot in our mouth because last year we said

02:42:15.510 --> 02:42:17.170
we're coming back for three, and we did.

02:42:17.350 --> 02:42:20.550
I'm sure somebody at the Grand Park Parade will open their mouths

02:42:20.550 --> 02:42:23.420
and say we're going to win four, but right now we're enjoying this third one

02:42:23.420 --> 02:42:25.660
because we've had to go through a lot of adversity this year

02:42:25.660 --> 02:42:28.340
with the book and all the injuries, and everybody counted us out.

02:42:28.660 --> 02:42:29.800
Our fans stayed behind us.

02:42:30.000 --> 02:42:33.430
We didn't win it in Chicago like we wanted to, but we won it on the road,

02:42:33.470 --> 02:42:35.410
and that's even sweeter because that shows you the kind of team we have.

02:42:35.510 --> 02:42:36.510
World champions once again.

02:42:36.670 --> 02:42:37.910
Congratulations on a great season.

02:42:38.070 --> 02:42:40.510
Stacey King, Chicago, number one.

02:42:40.510 --> 02:42:40.610
We're coming back.

02:42:40.750 --> 02:42:41.490
Get ready to party.

02:42:41.610 --> 02:42:42.190
We're coming back.

02:42:42.210 --> 02:42:42.870
We love you, baby.

02:42:43.570 --> 02:42:44.510
Happy Father's Day.

02:42:45.470 --> 02:42:46.370
Back to you guys.

02:42:46.910 --> 02:42:48.890
All right, Michael, thank you very much.

02:42:49.090 --> 02:42:51.270
Stacey King having to get in the last word.

02:42:51.690 --> 02:42:54.230
By the way, Michael Jordan set another record,

02:42:54.330 --> 02:42:57.270
averaging 41 points in the six-game series.

02:42:57.740 --> 02:42:59.480
How about the Chicago Bulls?

02:42:59.480 --> 02:42:59.980
as he scored 30.

02:43:00.000 --> 02:43:29.960
33 tonight and Michael the unanimous MVP that says a lot because Charles Barkley also had a great series well Michael with the average of 41 points the way he carried the team he set the tempo the things he did certainly more than his scoring Michael set up his teammates with passes he rebound like tonight he got eight key rebounds and when the team was kind of slowing down so he's done a tremendous job and very easily could have been the most valuable player in the league this year besides playoffs Bulls also hitting 10 three-pointers there were 10 of 14

02:43:30.000 --> 02:43:31.420
That is also a finals record.

02:43:31.540 --> 02:43:35.300
You're taking a look at some video right now of Forest Park,

02:43:35.300 --> 02:43:39.020
not far from our Sports Channel Report studios here in Oak Park.

02:43:40.450 --> 02:43:43.650
And let's hope the fans are going to stand to control, right?

02:43:43.830 --> 02:43:44.630
Well, I hope so.

02:43:44.850 --> 02:43:46.510
You know, it's great to win championships,

02:43:46.670 --> 02:43:51.800
but it's also responsible to not harm each other and tear up the city

02:43:51.800 --> 02:43:54.500
and be responsible for what you do out there.

02:43:55.330 --> 02:43:56.850
Once again, it's only a basketball game.

02:43:56.970 --> 02:43:59.910
It's great we won the world championship and very easily can win a fourth win.

02:44:00.000 --> 02:44:02.760
But please, just be cool out there.

02:44:03.050 --> 02:44:04.270
Well, it looks cool right now.

02:44:04.430 --> 02:44:05.510
I mean, they let people drive by.

02:44:05.670 --> 02:44:07.870
The police officers look like they have it under control.

02:44:07.990 --> 02:44:09.170
People just happy, cheering.

02:44:09.230 --> 02:44:12.190
Let's hope it is like that around the rest of the city.

02:44:12.310 --> 02:44:14.350
But our advice, stay in tonight, folks.

02:44:14.430 --> 02:44:14.850
Have fun.

02:44:14.950 --> 02:44:16.330
Keep watching here on Sports Channel.

02:44:16.600 --> 02:44:20.500
We are far from being through with our coverage right here.

02:44:20.640 --> 02:44:22.820
Johnny Red Kerr and Julie Jettleson, Mike Goldberg,

02:44:22.860 --> 02:44:24.780
reporting from the America West Arena.

02:44:24.940 --> 02:44:27.200
I'm Steve Cashel here along with Norm Van Leer.

02:44:27.540 --> 02:44:29.970
And we're going to go to a break right now.

02:44:30.000 --> 02:44:32.560
now and as we go to a break we're gonna take a look at an interesting graphic

02:44:32.560 --> 02:44:38.750
right here Eastern Conference champions are 13 and 1 on the road the last five

02:44:38.750 --> 02:44:43.200
years in the NBA Finals when we come back we're gonna hear from Danny Ainge and

02:44:43.200 --> 02:44:47.680
Scotty Williams we continue here with postgame coverage Bulls winning the

02:44:47.680 --> 02:44:48.480
three-peat

02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:02.880
Look right now at some more statistics right here.

02:45:03.020 --> 02:45:04.100
A couple of finals records.

02:45:04.280 --> 02:45:08.100
Michael averaging 41 points per game in the six-game series against the Suns.

02:45:08.200 --> 02:45:14.060
The Bulls tonight hitting a finals record 10 three-pointers, 10 of 14 from the three-point line.

02:45:14.120 --> 02:45:16.600
And the Bulls only scoring 12 points in the fourth quarter.

02:45:16.780 --> 02:45:18.560
That is also an NBA finals record.

02:45:18.640 --> 02:45:23.940
Look at the Suns shooting 39%, while the Bulls shot 47%.

02:45:23.940 --> 02:45:25.360
Back to Norm Van Leer.

02:45:25.460 --> 02:45:26.380
Norm, I've got a question for you.

02:45:26.500 --> 02:45:29.260
How special is it for you, being a former player?

02:45:29.260 --> 02:45:29.920
or you play with this.

02:45:30.000 --> 02:45:35.240
organization for a good seven years and being a former player now uh what's it like what's what's

02:45:35.240 --> 02:45:40.860
the gut reaction right here you have to feel a real proud sense of uh steve i'm i'm as happy as they

02:45:40.860 --> 02:45:46.730
are i'm just trying to keep my cool here on this on the set you know uh it's i'm a bull you know i'm

02:45:46.730 --> 02:45:51.690
nothing else but a bull and anything they do good or bad i feel it you know and winning like this

02:45:51.690 --> 02:45:56.310
has just been great and i gotta say thank you to the bulls for a lot of things it's brought my life

02:45:56.310 --> 02:45:59.530
back on the upbeat. I'm doing a lot of things such as being here.

02:46:00.000 --> 02:46:02.820
And getting around town, doing a lot of speaking engagements and appearances.

02:46:03.220 --> 02:46:06.100
And if the Bulls are not winning, I guarantee you it would not be happening.

02:46:06.280 --> 02:46:07.740
So it's been fun.

02:46:07.840 --> 02:46:08.920
This is the greatest city in the world.

02:46:09.020 --> 02:46:09.540
I love it.

02:46:09.640 --> 02:46:15.100
And you can't help but feel great and proud of what they've accomplished and done.

02:46:15.220 --> 02:46:18.260
And my hat's off to the whole organization, Jerry Krause and everyone else.

02:46:18.460 --> 02:46:20.500
By the way, Jerry, I wear a size 9 ring.

02:46:20.960 --> 02:46:22.440
Let's hope Norm will get in the ring.

02:46:22.500 --> 02:46:22.860
We'll see.

02:46:22.960 --> 02:46:26.800
But also, Norm, whenever we're at the stadium, before the games are, you know,

02:46:26.860 --> 02:46:28.600
we spend a lot of time at the stadium during the finals,

02:46:28.640 --> 02:46:29.960
at least getting to the first half of games.

02:46:30.000 --> 02:46:36.800
A lot of people came up to you and said, don't forget, Walker, Love, Borwinkle, you guys set the groundwork, Van Leer.

02:46:36.920 --> 02:46:39.200
It's got to really feel good, though, when people say that.

02:46:39.460 --> 02:46:47.560
Well, there's one thing you have to do and you feel proud of, and these people that are on this championship team with these last three world championship victories,

02:46:47.620 --> 02:46:52.120
they will always, always remember, you know, just looking at that ring and what they have accomplished.

02:46:52.360 --> 02:46:55.920
And believe me, it's not going to hit them two years later what they've done.

02:46:56.460 --> 02:46:59.800
And I guarantee you in my living, and I've been retired,

02:47:00.000 --> 02:47:05.720
13 years now. Still, we haven't won a championship as my own individual person, you know, going for

02:47:05.720 --> 02:47:10.440
something like that. But man, it's just the greatest thing to be able to play and do the best you can

02:47:10.440 --> 02:47:14.040
while you're out there playing. I live it and relive it all the time because the people of this

02:47:14.040 --> 02:47:18.010
city won't let you forget. And it's one thing about this city, if you work hard and do what you have

02:47:18.010 --> 02:47:23.880
to do and come to work every day, people appreciate you the rest of your life. That's all I can ask

02:47:23.880 --> 02:47:27.980
and it's just great. All right, we're going to go back down to the America West Arena. After the

02:47:27.980 --> 02:47:29.920
the game. Our reporters caught up with Scott Williams.

02:47:30.000 --> 02:47:38.440
and Danny Ainge you know it's been a great great run for me I came into this

02:47:38.440 --> 02:47:41.220
league undrafted most people didn't think I would stick around long enough to

02:47:41.820 --> 02:47:44.660
pick up a you know two or three paychecks and here I am with three

02:47:44.660 --> 02:47:48.460
championship rings is it better this way winning this way not winning back in

02:47:48.460 --> 02:47:51.760
Chicago because this is the hard way it's difficult you know it'd be nice to

02:47:51.760 --> 02:47:54.180
be able to jump up and down on that score so we will again and celebrate with

02:47:54.180 --> 02:47:57.800
our fans like we did in the old barn last year and Scott doesn't have that

02:47:57.800 --> 02:47:58.540
many years left.

02:48:00.000 --> 02:48:01.180
But we're a better road team.

02:48:01.360 --> 02:48:03.620
We get away from Chicago, and we focus well.

02:48:03.780 --> 02:48:04.400
We stick together.

02:48:04.740 --> 02:48:06.380
And it obviously showed tonight.

02:48:06.520 --> 02:48:09.340
You know, we didn't start pointing fingers when we lost an eight-point lead.

02:48:10.080 --> 02:48:11.420
We continue to play well.

02:48:11.580 --> 02:48:14.120
We continue to play – well, not well, but we continue to play hard anyway.

02:48:14.380 --> 02:48:17.520
And, you know, good things happen to those teams that keep gutting it out.

02:48:17.620 --> 02:48:18.680
Rough fourth quarter.

02:48:18.760 --> 02:48:20.460
Did you guys think you were staying here all week?

02:48:20.900 --> 02:48:21.300
Yeah.

02:48:22.380 --> 02:48:23.720
I was like, it's too hot.

02:48:24.460 --> 02:48:25.640
It's too damn hot here.

02:48:25.760 --> 02:48:28.420
And just wanted to try to make something happen.

02:48:28.420 --> 02:48:29.980
I mean, we didn't know, but, you know, you got to.

02:48:30.000 --> 02:48:33.100
to keep the faith, and John Paxson with a big three-pointer, I'll tell you, I love that

02:48:33.100 --> 02:48:39.020
guy, a guy who goes through two knee surgeries, loses a starting position, never complains

02:48:39.020 --> 02:48:43.900
one minute, works hard and practices every day, helped B.J. Armstrong and the rest of

02:48:43.900 --> 02:48:48.720
us who are getting more playing time coming up off the bench, the ultimate professional

02:48:48.720 --> 02:48:52.500
in my opinion, and it's rewarding to see him have his big day today.

02:48:52.680 --> 02:48:57.100
Scott, Jerry Krause said the best $100,000 this organization ever spent was getting

02:48:57.100 --> 02:48:59.100
John Paxson on that particular deal.

02:49:00.000 --> 02:49:01.640
It's a good time for you to see Jerry Krause.

02:49:04.520 --> 02:49:05.700
He's in a good mood right now.

02:49:05.940 --> 02:49:06.500
He's in a very good mood.

02:49:06.840 --> 02:49:07.880
He's passing out the money.

02:49:08.040 --> 02:49:09.080
He's passing out the money like there's no tomorrow.

02:49:09.080 --> 02:49:09.940
Anybody got a pin?

02:49:10.080 --> 02:49:11.220
Yeah, I got a pin on our contract.

02:49:11.560 --> 02:49:12.740
You know, I'm a free agent.

02:49:12.940 --> 02:49:15.700
And, you know, things are going to work themselves out.

02:49:15.760 --> 02:49:16.820
You know, I love this city.

02:49:17.040 --> 02:49:18.780
It's always welcoming from day one.

02:49:18.860 --> 02:49:19.320
I've been here.

02:49:19.400 --> 02:49:21.920
I've always got the support from fans writing me letters to keep my head,

02:49:22.080 --> 02:49:23.340
continue to play hard and work hard.

02:49:23.500 --> 02:49:25.280
And, you know, I'd love to be back here.

02:49:25.440 --> 02:49:28.660
And I just got to let go right now and, you know, let God guide me.

02:49:28.660 --> 02:49:29.880
I would imagine.

02:49:30.000 --> 02:49:33.520
Danny, a lot of the Bulls felt until John Paxton made that shot,

02:49:33.540 --> 02:49:34.480
they'd be here all week.

02:49:34.870 --> 02:49:37.930
Was that the feeling on your guys' part, too, that it was going to Game 7?

02:49:38.710 --> 02:49:39.030
Absolutely.

02:49:39.390 --> 02:49:41.090
We had a four-point lead, three possessions.

02:49:41.630 --> 02:49:42.790
Couldn't get the ball in the basket.

02:49:42.790 --> 02:49:45.530
If we're scoring any of those three possessions, the game's over.

02:49:46.520 --> 02:49:50.610
And, yeah, I felt like it was going to Game 7 all along.

02:49:52.070 --> 02:49:53.380
What changed?

02:49:53.620 --> 02:49:55.920
Did the wind just totally go out of your sails at that point?

02:49:56.080 --> 02:49:57.880
No, I don't think the wind went out of our sails.

02:49:57.980 --> 02:49:59.980
I think that, you know, they made a great job.

02:50:00.000 --> 02:50:06.520
play we had a couple breakdowns we had really good looks at the basket shots just didn't fall

02:50:06.520 --> 02:50:10.820
I don't think there was any wind out of our sail I think that's just basketball sometimes the shots

02:50:10.820 --> 02:50:17.480
don't go sometimes guys make great plays and you know I don't think that I don't think there's

02:50:17.480 --> 02:50:23.710
anything other than they made the shot when they needed to and we missed the shots when we had it

02:50:23.710 --> 02:50:27.410
I heard you talking earlier and you were saying that you blame a lot of the loss in this series

02:50:27.410 --> 02:50:29.350
early for the first two games and certainly not

02:50:29.350 --> 02:50:29.970
for this one of those.

02:50:30.000 --> 02:50:34.000
last one, which you guys played well. I think we played well. I'm just saying that this one,

02:50:34.040 --> 02:50:42.100
I think that we should have won this game and taken it to a game seven. But, you know, things like

02:50:42.100 --> 02:50:47.120
that happen in basketball. You lose when you should win sometimes. And we just used up our

02:50:47.120 --> 02:50:54.240
quota of room for air and to make up for a shot like that, that ends your season. And we used up

02:50:54.240 --> 02:50:59.340
all our games one and game two. Is it a more bitter pill to swallow than maybe previous losses

02:50:59.340 --> 02:50:59.880
That's a good point.

02:51:00.000 --> 02:51:07.620
for you? Yeah. Why? Because I feel that we're better. I've never lost at the end of a season

02:51:08.560 --> 02:51:14.380
when, well there's been a couple times, but last year we lost to Chicago and I felt they were

02:51:14.380 --> 02:51:19.520
better. There was no question they were the best team. And you tip your hats to them and say great

02:51:19.520 --> 02:51:24.740
year. And this year I don't feel that way. I feel that we should have won game six and I believe

02:51:24.740 --> 02:51:29.460
we would have won game seven. So that's a little bit tougher to swallow when you lose, when you

02:51:29.460 --> 02:51:29.860
Thank you.

02:51:30.000 --> 02:51:36.110
just as good or better. So Danny Ainge certainly not backing down off his comments that he said

02:51:36.110 --> 02:51:40.350
earlier. He always felt the Suns were the better team. He's told reporters that and even tonight

02:51:40.350 --> 02:51:44.210
even after the three-peat he still maintains that. Now while none of the Bulls will tell you that

02:51:44.210 --> 02:51:49.880
they will admit they played a worse game than the Suns and that might be even a bitter more bitter

02:51:49.880 --> 02:51:53.900
pill for Ainge to swallow. Yeah the Bulls obviously feel fortunate to be out of here and

02:51:53.900 --> 02:51:57.860
be the champions again and you and I talked about it I believe after the triple overtime game we

02:51:57.860 --> 02:51:59.600
I talked about it again after game four.

02:52:00.000 --> 02:52:03.760
which the Bulls won, how the Suns seemed to feel like they were not going to go away.

02:52:03.880 --> 02:52:07.620
Their confidence never really faltered, albeit losing two at home to start the series and

02:52:07.620 --> 02:52:08.600
then being down 3-1.

02:52:08.800 --> 02:52:10.820
Well, this destiny thing, they really mean.

02:52:10.900 --> 02:52:14.460
Charles Barkley can laugh about it, and Michael can say he reads a different Bible, but they

02:52:14.460 --> 02:52:15.520
felt they were the team.

02:52:15.620 --> 02:52:18.540
Kevin Johnson said he thought Chicago was a crumbling dynasty.

02:52:18.960 --> 02:52:20.940
Clearly, the Bulls proved tonight they're not crumbling.

02:52:21.570 --> 02:52:25.230
And neither did Horace Grant, albeit he said it was one of the toughest moments of his

02:52:25.230 --> 02:52:26.750
life, one of the toughest of his career.

02:52:27.070 --> 02:52:28.170
I'm speaking of Game 5.

02:52:28.170 --> 02:52:29.890
Horace came back tonight, did not.

02:52:30.000 --> 02:52:34.100
contribute offensively like he wanted, but he worked the boards tremendously. He did, and he

02:52:34.100 --> 02:52:39.680
was very clutch in the end. I mean, locking Kevin Johnson's shot. Yeah, it came down to Horace Grant.

02:52:39.780 --> 02:52:43.100
As a matter of fact, I caught up with Horace Grant as the Bulls departed the locker room now

02:52:43.100 --> 02:52:47.940
about 25 minutes ago. Horace out to start the celebration. Actually, he had already started it.

02:52:48.000 --> 02:52:52.940
Here's some of Horace's final thoughts on the championship. Lock room with Horace Grant. All

02:52:52.940 --> 02:52:56.380
season long, you've been able to put things in perspective. Can you put this in perspective for

02:52:56.380 --> 02:52:59.440
It was a hard, grueling series.

02:53:00.000 --> 02:53:05.820
But we overcame a lot of obstacles and controversy, and we came together as a team.

02:53:06.080 --> 02:53:09.400
As frustrating as Game 5 was, this is so much better, isn't it?

02:53:09.620 --> 02:53:12.220
Oh, you know, I'd rather have this any day than Game 5.

02:53:12.760 --> 02:53:17.020
You know, Game 5 was very frustrating, but my teammates really pulled me through it.

02:53:17.220 --> 02:53:19.940
Today was a day where everybody seemed to do their chores.

02:53:20.060 --> 02:53:22.000
You didn't get a lot of points, but you were on the boards.

02:53:22.300 --> 02:53:25.440
Scotty got some shots, Scotty got some rebounds, Michael got some assists.

02:53:25.640 --> 02:53:28.340
It was a roll day, and John packs in the role player outside jumper.

02:53:28.340 --> 02:53:29.980
Well, whenever we come together...

02:53:30.000 --> 02:53:35.040
like that and everyone contribute uh knowing their role roles and doing their roles uh we

02:53:35.040 --> 02:53:39.580
win championships and this one still settling in right now i know you just had some quiet time

02:53:39.580 --> 02:53:44.420
with some of your family is this one as good better even better than the other ones or equal

02:53:44.420 --> 02:53:50.400
this one is much sweeter because of uh the controversy that we went through and uh winning

02:53:50.400 --> 02:53:56.410
here in phoenix it was the best team in uh in the league uh during the regular season and uh

02:53:56.410 --> 02:53:58.750
They got a guy named Charles Barkley.

02:53:58.970 --> 02:53:59.830
You know, that's why.

02:54:00.000 --> 02:54:03.960
makes it much sweeter. You're looking right in the camera with that answer. You got a message to give, don't you?

02:54:04.620 --> 02:54:07.740
Charles, you owe me dinner, but it'll be in Chicago.

02:54:08.060 --> 02:54:12.000
Final question. You've talked a lot, Horace, about the fact that you might not mind being

02:54:12.000 --> 02:54:15.920
a superstar in another team, winning as many championships, but look at this right now. How can you

02:54:15.920 --> 02:54:19.880
pass this opportunity up? Well, you know, I'm not going to

02:54:19.880 --> 02:54:23.440
answer that. I'm not going to start with that, but the thing is, I'm going to just savor this moment.

02:54:23.640 --> 02:54:28.790
Thank you for all your help offseason. Congratulations. Alright, three. Three indeed as is.

02:54:28.790 --> 02:54:29.930
This is the last question I asked Horace.

02:54:30.000 --> 02:54:33.840
Grant, as you heard, Julie, about the fact that he said he'll go to a lesser team, be the superstar,

02:54:33.900 --> 02:54:35.380
but how do you pass up three championships?

02:54:36.040 --> 02:54:38.960
Or four, as Michael Jordan is already talking about him.

02:54:39.020 --> 02:54:39.440
Can you imagine?

02:54:39.700 --> 02:54:44.510
But the man of the evening besides Michael Jordan, who usually always is and still will be,

02:54:44.890 --> 02:54:45.810
John Paxson.

02:54:45.950 --> 02:54:47.170
The reporters were all around him.

02:54:47.270 --> 02:54:52.870
He had that big boy next door grin and really a moment for him that he will remember forever.

02:54:53.150 --> 02:54:57.480
And the nice thing, being a Bulls fan, is that John Paxson, working with the team,

02:54:57.520 --> 02:54:59.660
is always the one who seems to be most cooperative.

02:54:59.660 --> 02:54:59.980
All

02:55:00.000 --> 02:55:03.320
He's always a first-class guy, goes through a season, when he loses his starting position,

02:55:03.440 --> 02:55:04.600
starts out with knee surgery.

02:55:04.680 --> 02:55:05.620
The knee was never right.

02:55:05.700 --> 02:55:07.400
It was a very frustrating year for Paxson.

02:55:07.420 --> 02:55:08.660
I think it ended apropos.

02:55:08.840 --> 02:55:13.240
He was so good in Game 5, didn't mean anything, but he was good enough to win it in Game 6.

02:55:13.950 --> 02:55:15.170
Paxson's had the worst season.

02:55:15.430 --> 02:55:19.050
I mean, he had that knee surgery, and it seemed like every game, it would bang in the knee.

02:55:19.150 --> 02:55:22.830
It's like that sore elbow you keep hitting, and he was really frustrated, but he never

02:55:22.830 --> 02:55:23.670
let that show.

02:55:23.950 --> 02:55:26.350
He hit the big shots, and you talk to Michael Jordan about it.

02:55:26.390 --> 02:55:29.050
Michael said he knew all along John Paxson was hitting that shot.

02:55:29.050 --> 02:55:29.970
But I as John

02:55:30.000 --> 02:55:35.560
Paxton was he so sure? I think every kid who's ever been in a park or in a

02:55:35.560 --> 02:55:40.620
driveway or in his backyard has taken shots to win games and I have a six

02:55:40.620 --> 02:55:46.300
year old son Ryan who does it every day and he has to make shots at the buzzer

02:55:46.300 --> 02:55:52.500
so I'm just I I'm sure that I'm I know I'm live I've lived out the fantasy was

02:55:52.500 --> 02:55:58.160
mine when I was a young person but I don't know what it means or how it feels

02:55:58.160 --> 02:55:59.960
I think that'll happen

02:56:00.000 --> 02:56:24.600
over time. Did you know it was going in, John? Did I know it was going in? I'm going to tell you right now that I certainly did. It felt good when it left my hands, but it's just a reaction. You're not thinking of that. You're thinking about catching it and shooting it. And when it went in, my first reaction was to look at the shot clock and see how much time was left. To be very honest, I wish there had been no time left on the clock rather than 3.9.

02:56:24.600 --> 02:56:29.650
But 3.9 was not enough time for the Phoenix Suns to win this basketball game.

02:56:30.000 --> 02:56:34.000
course of Game 7. And now, as you mentioned, you look towards the future. You wonder about the

02:56:34.000 --> 02:56:38.640
future of a Rodney McRae. You wonder if, indeed, Tony Kukoc will be solidified and be a member of

02:56:38.640 --> 02:56:42.060
this team next year. There are some question marks, and there are some places the Bulls will

02:56:42.060 --> 02:56:45.780
want to improve in the offseason. Bill Cartwright has an option here on his contract. You wonder

02:56:45.780 --> 02:56:49.600
where Scott Williams will be. You wonder how much of the nucleus of this team that's won three

02:56:49.600 --> 02:56:53.460
championships will remain together. But I don't think it's a topic the Bulls really want to talk

02:56:53.460 --> 02:56:58.040
about tonight or really even think about because they're all soaked with champagne, and this is

02:56:58.040 --> 02:56:59.980
their moment. Yeah, they won't talk about the future.

02:57:00.000 --> 02:57:03.620
as far as improving the team, and they won't talk about the foreplay, the forepeat,

02:57:03.700 --> 02:57:04.780
whatever you want to call it right now.

02:57:04.900 --> 02:57:06.660
They won't talk about that fourth championship,

02:57:06.800 --> 02:57:08.500
although you said Michael did just a little bit, huh?

02:57:08.840 --> 02:57:09.980
Michael could not resist.

02:57:10.240 --> 02:57:14.020
I mean, he went into this year saying that this was going to be much easier than last year,

02:57:14.060 --> 02:57:15.760
and he said today, he put his foot in his mouth.

02:57:15.920 --> 02:57:18.120
This was the hardest thing he's probably ever done,

02:57:18.200 --> 02:57:22.760
but I would never question Michael Jordan trying to do something else he hasn't done.

02:57:22.960 --> 02:57:24.460
Yeah, there is no doubt about that.

02:57:24.460 --> 02:57:25.900
You speak about cherishing the moment.

02:57:26.040 --> 02:57:27.840
Will Perdue, it had to be a frustrating series.

02:57:27.840 --> 02:57:29.680
He didn't get the minutes that he would have liked to.

02:57:29.680 --> 02:57:29.700
Thank you.

02:57:30.000 --> 02:57:32.760
but he was still jubilant and enjoying yet another championship.

02:57:33.100 --> 02:57:35.040
These things, the rings, stand forever.

02:57:35.040 --> 02:57:36.540
My conversation with Will Perdue.

02:57:38.640 --> 02:57:39.700
More here from the locker room.

02:57:39.760 --> 02:57:43.220
Will Perdue, apropos, I think, for John Paxson to hit the last shot.

02:57:43.340 --> 02:57:45.400
Such a great contributor to this club for so many years.

02:57:45.660 --> 02:57:49.760
I mean, he always has been, and it's kind of spooky how, you know,

02:57:49.820 --> 02:57:53.400
he comes back, and every year in the playoffs he steps up big.

02:57:53.540 --> 02:57:56.920
And, you know, unfortunately that effort he had in Game 5 kind of went to waste,

02:57:56.980 --> 02:57:58.180
but he didn't let it bother him.

02:57:58.420 --> 02:57:59.400
He came back tonight.

02:58:00.000 --> 02:58:02.780
He hit a few shots before the big one, but the big one is what counts.

02:58:03.060 --> 02:58:05.780
Why did it seem to be easier to win on the road in this series?

02:58:06.800 --> 02:58:07.580
I wish we knew.

02:58:07.740 --> 02:58:09.440
I mean, that's something we've got to ask the Suns

02:58:09.440 --> 02:58:10.980
and see what they have to say about it.

02:58:11.080 --> 02:58:16.400
But today before the game, it was pretty quiet in the locker room,

02:58:16.420 --> 02:58:18.600
which is uncharacteristic of this team.

02:58:19.140 --> 02:58:21.760
I mean, we knew coming out here it was very businesslike.

02:58:22.380 --> 02:58:25.960
There were, you know, there's a lot of wives and spouses at home right now

02:58:25.960 --> 02:58:28.800
that aren't very happy with the fact they couldn't make it.

02:58:28.860 --> 02:58:29.520
But it was, you know.

02:58:30.000 --> 02:58:33.280
We knew we were coming out here for business, you know, for one thing and for one thing only.

02:58:33.480 --> 02:58:36.300
And we wanted to win this thing on Sunday, today, and just get it over with

02:58:36.300 --> 02:58:38.460
because the last thing we want to do is hang out in Phoenix for three more days.

02:58:38.580 --> 02:58:40.900
Yeah, for obvious reasons, you did not want a game seven.

02:58:41.500 --> 02:58:44.160
Indeed, it would have given them a chance with a victory to steal the championship.

02:58:44.420 --> 02:58:44.920
Yeah, it would have.

02:58:45.040 --> 02:58:48.640
But honestly, I don't think that, you know, they could have won, you know, three in a row.

02:58:48.760 --> 02:58:50.080
And I think that would have been very difficult.

02:58:50.260 --> 02:58:53.940
And I think by, you know, you can tell by the way they played down the stretch that they got,

02:58:54.060 --> 02:58:55.340
they were just as tight as we were.

02:58:55.800 --> 02:58:57.680
You know, if they hit their shots, they'd probably win the game.

02:58:57.760 --> 02:58:59.620
We come down and hit our shots and had some big stops.

02:58:59.780 --> 02:58:59.840
Thank you.

02:59:00.000 --> 02:59:02.320
Some people would say it was a frustrating series for Will Perdue,

02:59:02.400 --> 02:59:04.300
didn't get as many minutes as I think you would have liked to,

02:59:04.380 --> 02:59:06.620
but throughout the playoffs, Will, everybody contributed.

02:59:06.820 --> 02:59:10.080
You were big in the Atlanta series, so it is a team effort to get to a championship, isn't it?

02:59:10.180 --> 02:59:10.880
I mean, it really is.

02:59:11.000 --> 02:59:14.760
I mean, Michael, you know, he didn't have one of the big games that we were kind of looking for tonight,

02:59:14.840 --> 02:59:18.270
but, you know, other guys stepped up, and, you know, fortunately, you know,

02:59:18.370 --> 02:59:20.910
Horace, even though he didn't play well, he had the big block at the end of the game.

02:59:21.030 --> 02:59:23.730
So it's those type of things where you try to keep a positive attitude,

02:59:23.730 --> 02:59:27.490
and you never know when the coach is going to call on you, and, you know, the way Pax is going,

02:59:27.510 --> 02:59:29.970
he was kind of, you know, disappointed with the fact his knee never got.

02:59:30.000 --> 02:59:33.620
better and he's you know everybody made the big controversy about he should be starting instead of

02:59:33.620 --> 02:59:37.380
bj etc etc but you know he did his job coming off the bench and he knew what he was doing and again

02:59:37.380 --> 02:59:40.700
how about the teach once you think he's gone once you think he's old he comes up and hits the big

02:59:40.700 --> 02:59:44.260
shots yeah i mean i was funny i was talking to bill kind of ribbing him a little bit that now

02:59:44.260 --> 02:59:48.160
that he's won his third title he can retire and he said well he's just glad he made it through the

02:59:48.160 --> 02:59:51.520
third title because he said if we played wednesday he didn't know if he'd make it or not what do you

02:59:51.520 --> 02:59:55.160
think is the future here in chicago for will purdue you know i really can't tell i mean that's

02:59:55.160 --> 02:59:59.140
it's a big decision right now it's just uh it depends on what management wants to do a lot

02:59:59.140 --> 02:59:59.980
that has to do with whether Bill

03:00:00.000 --> 03:00:01.440
wants to come back or not.

03:00:02.220 --> 03:00:05.100
So I imagine for me, even though October comes pretty soon,

03:00:05.200 --> 03:00:05.980
it's going to be a long summer.

03:00:06.300 --> 03:00:07.920
Regardless of what happens, enjoy the summer

03:00:07.920 --> 03:00:10.120
and those three rings that are on all three of your fingers.

03:00:10.260 --> 03:00:11.920
Three World Championships for Will Perdue.

03:00:12.200 --> 03:00:13.540
What a great guy from Vanderbilt.

03:00:13.640 --> 03:00:16.680
He has another championship, as do the Bulls more postgame after this.

03:00:17.730 --> 03:00:19.870
Back in the Bulls locker room, Will Perdue just said

03:00:19.870 --> 03:00:23.480
that the talk about the three-peats started at the rally a year ago.

03:00:23.620 --> 03:00:26.120
We will, of course, have full rally coverage here on Sports Channel

03:00:26.120 --> 03:00:27.600
when the official details are mentioned.

03:00:27.700 --> 03:00:29.980
But all in all, a great season for the Chicago Bulls.

03:00:30.000 --> 03:00:32.740
one in which there were a lot of questions raised about the fact

03:00:32.740 --> 03:00:35.140
if they could three-peat, they didn't have the best record,

03:00:35.280 --> 03:00:38.020
they didn't have the home court advantage in the finals of the Eastern Conference

03:00:38.020 --> 03:00:41.800
or the NBA Finals, but somehow, someway, they're still the world champions.

03:00:42.020 --> 03:00:44.000
And that is not a thought lost on them.

03:00:44.140 --> 03:00:46.660
One of the striking things about tonight were the emotions.

03:00:46.840 --> 03:00:48.460
Horace Grant practically in tears.

03:00:48.600 --> 03:00:51.620
B.J. Armstrong, someone who was always so sturdy when you talked to him,

03:00:52.170 --> 03:00:53.190
very close to tears.

03:00:53.370 --> 03:00:56.970
Michael embracing Daryl Walker and Trent Tucker, the first ring for them.

03:00:57.090 --> 03:00:58.870
This is something really that they will cherish

03:00:58.870 --> 03:00:59.410
and something.

03:01:00.000 --> 03:01:01.580
that they may never see again.

03:01:02.080 --> 03:01:03.520
Julie, it was great memories this season.

03:01:03.600 --> 03:01:05.020
It ends with the best of them all, doesn't it?

03:01:05.730 --> 03:01:07.770
This is something that any reporter who would cover

03:01:07.770 --> 03:01:08.770
would never forget this either,

03:01:08.810 --> 03:01:10.870
despite all the champagne being soaked all over you.

03:01:11.030 --> 03:01:13.150
A great job done by the Chicago Bulls.

03:01:13.170 --> 03:01:14.390
Hope you've enjoyed the coverage tonight

03:01:14.390 --> 03:01:15.790
here from the America West Arena.

03:01:15.910 --> 03:01:17.190
Mike Goldberg, Julie Juttleson.

03:01:17.290 --> 03:01:19.970
Back to our Sports Channel Report studio, Stephen Norm.

03:01:20.290 --> 03:01:23.040
Looks like Mike and Julie got pretty dry, though.

03:01:23.260 --> 03:01:24.480
They look as dry as we are,

03:01:24.600 --> 03:01:26.940
but I'm sure it's a lot of fun in the locker room.

03:01:27.440 --> 03:01:29.980
Norm, are we crazy thinking about a four-peat?

03:01:30.760 --> 03:01:34.080
Not at all, and it's going to be brought up, no doubt about it.

03:01:34.180 --> 03:01:35.220
The team's still intact.

03:01:35.460 --> 03:01:40.830
The basic players are there when you have the Jordan, the Pippins, and the Horace Grant.

03:01:40.950 --> 03:01:44.170
We don't know, I guess, a question there, but as long as you've got Michael,

03:01:44.270 --> 03:01:45.510
there's a shot at winning another one.

03:01:45.650 --> 03:01:49.310
And so I think the team definitely has to make changes.

03:01:49.510 --> 03:01:56.020
I think of the three championships they have, Steve, this is the weakest team of the three, in my opinion.

03:01:56.300 --> 03:01:57.220
I think they had to struggle.

03:01:57.340 --> 03:01:58.620
Michael had to put in a lot more minutes.

03:01:58.620 --> 03:01:59.400
and

03:02:00.000 --> 03:02:01.160
you know, in that situation.

03:02:01.160 --> 03:02:04.160
I think this team has to improve from the bench a little bit.

03:02:04.360 --> 03:02:07.600
I think you certainly have to start shopping around looking for a center.

03:02:07.940 --> 03:02:09.880
And Cartwright's done the job, let's face it.

03:02:09.920 --> 03:02:12.720
Regardless what people and what the press may say about this gentleman,

03:02:12.720 --> 03:02:13.840
he's done the job.

03:02:13.880 --> 03:02:16.880
But you have to start looking at the age, the legs, start replacing him.

03:02:17.000 --> 03:02:20.520
And I think we have to come up with another score off that bench

03:02:20.520 --> 03:02:23.780
to help Michael when he's not in a game, pipping or whatever,

03:02:24.220 --> 03:02:25.880
to keep the pace with the Bulls.

03:02:25.920 --> 03:02:28.880
I think they have to make some big changes from the bench point of view.

03:02:28.880 --> 03:02:29.970
I was asking a student,

03:02:30.000 --> 03:02:35.320
Assistant Coach Johnny Bach, the question about a four-peat before Game 5 Friday night at the stadium.

03:02:35.320 --> 03:02:38.820
We sat down, and we'll show some of that interview this week on the Sports Channel Report.

03:02:38.980 --> 03:02:41.400
But Johnny told me, he said, we're going to get Tony Kukic.

03:02:41.580 --> 03:02:45.960
He says he might have gone among the top five in the NBA draft.

03:02:45.960 --> 03:02:47.340
We think he is that good.

03:02:47.520 --> 03:02:50.000
So the Bulls get possibly a top five draft pick.

03:02:50.060 --> 03:02:53.100
I think it might take him a year to get going.

03:02:53.240 --> 03:02:56.590
But John also said that he's going to have Phil Jackson as his coach.

03:02:56.690 --> 03:02:59.970
And there's no one better than Phil Jackson to get you ready for the grind of the NBA.

03:03:00.000 --> 03:03:05.480
And as long as they hold on to MJ, BJ, Scottie Pippen, and Horace Grant, I mean, I don't

03:03:05.480 --> 03:03:07.060
see this team backing down at all.

03:03:07.120 --> 03:03:09.940
I think they have something over the Blazers from last year, something over the Knicks

03:03:09.940 --> 03:03:13.420
from this year, and now certainly something over the Phoenix Suns.

